From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:38:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] rocket: rk3576: print the OUT_CVT shift only when it is
 overridden

The OUT_CVT shift was printed to stderr for every convolution of every
model while compiling, about 150 lines for a detection model, which
ends up in the journal of any service using the delegate. Print it only
together with the ROCKET_OUT_SHIFT_ABS override it is a diagnostic for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6ragSxZN7WKWgGsfgrMX1
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
index 12e8799..6cc6bdf 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
@@ -1384,16 +1384,17 @@ fill_regcmd_rk3576_normal(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
        * shift to an ABSOLUTE N (small N = max amplify, no negative-wrap risk),
        * to decide whether the zero-rail is a non-zero MAC crushed by requant
        * (output lights up as the shift drops) or a genuine empty MAC (stays out_zp
-       * across the whole sweep). Also prints the computed shift for reference.
+       * across the whole sweep). Then also prints the computed shift for reference.
        */
       const char *abs_s = getenv("ROCKET_OUT_SHIFT_ABS");
       uint32_t shift_val =
          abs_s ? (uint32_t)atoi(abs_s)
                : operation->rq_exact ? operation->rq_shift
                                      : (shift - 1 + rkt_out_shift_add());
-      fprintf(stderr,
-              "rocket: OUT_CVT computed_shift=%d scale=0x%x -> emitting shift=%u\n",
-              (int)shift - 1, cvt_scale, shift_val);
+      if (abs_s)
+         fprintf(stderr,
+                 "rocket: OUT_CVT computed_shift=%d scale=0x%x -> emitting shift=%u\n",
+                 (int)shift - 1, cvt_scale, shift_val);
       R_DPU(0x40b4, shift_val); /* OUT_CVT shift (+0x80 de-scale) */
    }
    R_DPU(0x40b8, (dw ? 4 : 2) * plane - ow * win_orows);
